	"Description": "Four colors are available. \n<br />\n<br />The original base was made by @mwillemsenart (whose awesome art portfolio can be viewed here:\u00A0[url=https://margaretwillemsen.weebly.com/]https://margaretwillemsen.weebly.com/[/url])\u00A0for this Alpaca Mod\u00A0[url=http://https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/8515?tab=description][/url][url=https://community.playstarbound.com/resources/alpaca-mod-for-sheep.3652/]https://community.playstarbound.com/resources/alpaca-mod-for-sheep.3652/[/url]\n<br />\n<br />I highly recommend the Adopt 'n' Skin Mod. This will make using .png files as skin replacements easier as well as allow you to use multiple skins in the game at once as long as they use the correct naming convention.\u00A0\n<br />\uFEFF\n<br />The \"All Colors\" folder contains sprite sheets which are already named appropriately for Adopt 'n' Skin. If there are any issues with skins loading, try dropping the sprite sheets into the mod's asset folder directly without being sorted into their own separate folder(s). \n<br />\n<br />Adopt 'n' Skin can also help if you'd rather use these skins as a vanilla sheep reskin, just be sure to name them appropriately.\n<br />\n<br />This mod does not change the color of products collected from alpacas.",
